anizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chozabu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chozabu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chozabu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chozabu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-24T15:50:31Z","updated_at":"2025-07-24T15:50:31Z","body":"> Is it doing this if the window is set to `borderless`?\n\nSetting the window to `borderless` does fix the issue _but it didn't yesterday_ I first noticed the issue in a project which uses a borderless window. That and other projects with borderless windows no longer have this transparency issue.\n\nSince reporting this bug, I have at least:\n-updated to latest nvidia drivers\n-turned (nvidia settings) digital vibrance down to 50%, and back up to 60%\n-changed \"performance options\" to best performance, and back to best appearance (in system properties/advanced system settings)\n-turned nvidia overlay off, and back on\n\nThough I don't know which if any of these actions have made a difference, as I've only been testing on the project with a window that has a border.\n\nI'll test with both a regular and borderless window from now on","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3113988894/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]